# clausal: no-collect
# Sibling module that declares the SAME functor and also imports it.
#
# The -module export list registers fnm_verdict/2 with field names
# (STATUS, CITATIONS) and emits its guarded class block; the -import_from that
# follows rebinds the name to the exporter's directive-minted class, whose
# fields are ('arg_0', 'arg_1').  The fact below USED to be constructed with
# the LOCAL field names against the FOREIGN class and raise; heads for an
# imported functor are now emitted positionally, so the module body runs.
#
# Since 2026-09-24 the LOAD is refused: fnmismatch_schema only declares
# fnm_verdict/2 (-dynamic, no clauses), and supplying its clauses downstream
# (the "vocabulary-implements" idiom) was dropped.  Kept no-collect as the
# fixture showing that refusal -- not a field-name TypeError -- is what stops
# it (tests/test_functor_import_ordering.py,
# tests/test_functor_field_name_diagnostic.py).
-double_quotes(atom)
-module(fnmismatch_use, [fnm_verdict(STATUS, CITATIONS), fnm_chk(RESULT)])
-import_from(tests.fixtures.fnmismatch_schema, [fnm_verdict])

fnm_verdict("ok", [])

fnm_chk(R) <- fnm_verdict(R, C_UNUSED)
